invariant: INV-26
file: ct.h
catches: test/quic-builds.sh
reason: a build declares a TLS cipher suite whose AEAD is AES-GCM and
  ct.h stops refusing it without CH_AES_HW, so the suite takes the
  Makefile default, AES=soft. That build hands a traffic key to a cipher
  whose 256-byte S-box is indexed with the key: aes_expand_round_keys
  substitutes the key's own bytes before a block runs, sub_bytes
  substitutes counter ^ round_key once per round, and gcm_ghash inherits
  it because the hash subkey is aes_encrypt_block of a zero block. The
  fall back is silent -- every source compiles and every vector passes --
  so the compiler's refusal is the only check, and this edit removes it.

--- old
#else
#error "CH_SUITE_AES_GCM needs AES=hw or AES=extern: the AES=soft S-box is indexed with the key"
#endif
--- new
#endif
